First, let's find an expression for $\dfrac{d}{dx}[f(x)-3h(x)+1]$ in terms of $f'$ and $h'$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{d}{dx}[f(x)-3h(x)+1]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[f(x)]-\dfrac{d}{dx}[3h(x)]+\dfrac{d}{dx}(1)&&\gray{\text{Sum and difference rules}}
\\\\
&=f'(x)-3h'(x)+0&&\gray{\text{Constant and constant multiple rules}}
\end{align}$

So we found that $\dfrac{d}{dx}[f(x)-3h(x)+1]=f'(x)-3h'(x)$.
